doc:participation_mia_1995_04_20 a echr:Participation ;
    rdfs:label "participation: MIA in working-group appointment 20 April 1995"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasPartySide echr:SideInitiating ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "It transpires from the MIA’s report that, on 20 April 1995, the MIA had appointed a “working group” ( delovna skupina ) consisting of officers from the Slovenj Gradec Police and the MIA to assess the lawfulness of the procedures carried out by the Special Unit and the Slovenj Gradec Police."^^xsd:string ;
    echr:participatingParty doc:domesticAuthorityMinistryInternalAffairs .

doc:participation_mia_report_1995_11_15 a echr:Participation ;
    rdfs:label "participation: MIA in MIA report 15 November 1995"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasPartySide echr:SideInitiating ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "Further to the analysis of procedures and activities which had taken place on 4 and 5 April 1995, the working group established that all the measures and procedures were lawful and in accordance with legal powers and professional rules."^^xsd:string ;
    echr:participatingParty doc:domesticAuthorityMinistryInternalAffairs .

doc:participation_objection_applicant_1999_01_27 a echr:Participation ;
    rdfs:label "participation: applicant objection to indictment 27 January 1999"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasPartySide echr:SideInitiating ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "On 27 January 1999 the applicant filed an objection to the indictment."^^xsd:string ;
    echr:participatingParty doc:applicantMrAleksanderMatko .

doc:participation_officer_d_p_1995 a echr:Participation ;
    rdfs:label "participation: Officer D.P. in pre-trial investigation 1995"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasPartySide echr:SideUnknown ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "“At the critical time, we were conducting, in the territory of Slovenj Gradec Police, an operation to investigate organised crime. (...) In front of the Hotel Pohorje, a group of people was noticed which included M.A. and Aleksander Matko. One of the police patrols noticed that M.A. left with the motorcycle and they also saw when Aleksander Matko drove away. In fact, everything happened very quickly (...). We placed vehicles at different locations (...). Our official vehicle, which I was driving, received a message that a white Golf was being driven by a person believed to be Aleksander Matko (...). We decided to stop him in order to search the car since there was a suspicion that he was armed.”"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:participatingParty doc:officerDP .

doc:participation_officer_i_g_1995 a echr:Participation ;
    rdfs:label "participation: Officer I.G. in pre-trial investigation 1995"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasPartySide echr:SideUnknown ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "Another officer from the Slovenj Gradec Police, I.G., who had arrived at the scene with the officers of the Special Unit and was also questioned in the criminal investigation, stated that there were 20 officers of the Special Unit and Slovenj Gradec Police at the scene, and that five of them had had direct contact with the applicant."^^xsd:string ;
    echr:participatingParty doc:officerIG .

doc:participation_officer_m_f_1995 a echr:Participation ;
    rdfs:label "participation: Officer M.F. in pre-trial investigation 1995"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasPartySide echr:SideUnknown ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "“We had information about individuals who were suspected members of that [criminal] organisation, and one of them was Aleksander Matko, whom I did not know since I am from Maribor, but I knew him from photographs. (...) We were on one of the streets of Slovenj Gradec when we received information that the car of Aleksander Matko had been seen and that our colleagues had tried to stop him, but he would not stop despite warnings.”"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:participatingParty doc:officerMF .

doc:participation_oral_applicant_1995_04_07 a echr:Participation ;
