doc:participation_questioning_applicant_1997_04_08 a echr:Participation ;
    rdfs:label "participation: applicant questioned by investigating judge 8 April 1997"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasPartySide echr:SideResponding ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "On 8 April 1997 the investigating judge questioned the applicant. The applicant denied having committed any offence and complained that he had been beaten and ill-treated by the police. He pointed out that he had medical reports proving his injuries. The reports were included in the file."^^xsd:string ;
    echr:participatingParty doc:applicantMrAleksanderMatko .

doc:participation_written_applicant_1995_05_15 a echr:Participation ;
    rdfs:label "participation: applicant in written complaint 15 May 1995"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasPartySide echr:SideInitiating ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "On 15 May 1995 the applicant lodged, through his lawyer, a written criminal complaint ( kazenska ovadba ) with the Slovenj Gradec Police against unidentified police officers for causing minor bodily harm ( lahka telesna poškodba ) and an unlawful deprivation of liberty ( protipraven odvzem prostosti )."^^xsd:string ;
    echr:participatingParty doc:applicantMrAleksanderMatko .

doc:participation_written_slovenj_gradec_police_1995_05_15 a echr:Participation ;
    rdfs:label "participation: Slovenj Gradec Police in written complaint 15 May 1995"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasPartySide echr:SideResponding ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "On 15 May 1995 the applicant lodged, through his lawyer, a written criminal complaint ( kazenska ovadba ) with the Slovenj Gradec Police against unidentified police officers for causing minor bodily harm ( lahka telesna poškodba ) and an unlawful deprivation of liberty ( protipraven odvzem prostosti )."^^xsd:string ;
    echr:participatingParty doc:domesticAuthoritySlovenjGradecPolice .

doc:police_operation_1995_04_04_05 a echr:EnforcementAction ;
    rdfs:label "police operation 4-5 April 1995"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "About thirty people were arrested and injured during the two-day operation."^^xsd:string,
        "In addition, he stated that by the time a minute had gone by after the applicant was stopped, there were already four or five vehicles of the Slovenj Gradec Police and the Special Unit at the scene and that three or four officers arrived in each vehicle."^^xsd:string,
        "On 4 and 5 April 1995 a Special Unit ( Specialna enota ), which was under the direct control of the Ministry of Internal Affairs (\"the MIA\") in cooperation with officers from the Slovenj Gradec Internal Affairs Administration ( Uprava za notranje zadeve – hereinafter referred as the \"Slovenj Gradec Police\") undertook a large-scale operation against the activities of a criminal organisation presumed to be operating on the territory of the town of Slovenj Gradec."^^xsd:string .

doc:pretrial_detention_1995_04_05_06 a echr:PreTrialDetention ;
    rdfs:label "pre-trial detention 5-6 April 1995"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasCustodialMeasure echr:MeasurePoliceCustody ;
    echr:hasDetainee doc:applicantMrAleksanderMatko ;
    echr:hasDetentionEndDate "1995-04-06"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasDetentionStartDate "1995-04-05"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "**26.** On 6 April 1995, soon after his release, the applicant was admitted to the Slovenj Gradec General Hospital where he stayed until 7 p.m. The medical report, written by a doctor in that hospital, stated that the applicant had bruises on his head, but did not include any details of the injuries. The applicant was advised to rest for a few days."^^xsd:string,
        """**27.** Next day, 7 April 1995, the applicant sought medical aid in the Maribor General Hospital. There, he also explained to a doctor that on 5 April 1995 he had been beaten by unknown armed persons. The medical report of 7 April 1995 indicates several lesions, including:
- bruises on the right eye and a small amount of suffusion in the surrounding area;
- a haematoma on the left side of the forehead
- a painful nose;
- a 6 cm by 4 cm haematoma on the left shoulder;
- two 4-5 cm linear skin abrasions on the left side of the thorax;
- a child’s-hand-sized moderate oedema behind the right ear;
- an extensive haematoma on the left thigh.
The doctors had also suspected a fracture of the right temporal bone. The report of an x-ray examination on 19 April 1995 indicated that there was a hairline fracture ( fissur a)."""^^xsd:string,
        "He was brought to the Slovenj Gradec Police Station for having allegedly failed to comply with the police orders. He was questioned by the police and released on 6 April 1995 at approximately half past midnight."^^xsd:string .

